#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096616 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096416 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "5eaa00f8-0fd0-5de6-a7c0-965db6de3a5c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3630" :question/problem "Given that $y= \\log_4 x + \\ln x$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( \\log_4 x + \\ln x \\right)\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\log_4 x) + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\ln x )\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 4} + \\dfrac{1}{x}.\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}+\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{ln⁡4}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050711}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a1ef8d-83de-5766-9657-a3bfe0bb38dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094790} {:answer/id #uuid "0252fcd7-aeab-5761-8acd-d83247a91140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094791} {:answer/id #uuid "0ec8a347-f04f-5b31-b96a-f6161c05a063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094792} {:answer/id #uuid "3d77c43e-3716-58ad-bfa3-1b5969543ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094793} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1e92d9-bcf0-58ec-9823-44766ae56d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094794}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7f1d45b3-2a55-54df-9843-cd54e2302ddb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094789}] :question/id #uuid "0259cf05-81de-512b-a7bb-bd7b4b70d4e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-17373" :question/problem "Given that $y =-\\frac{3}{5}\\ln x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x = 1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9535bbe-8473-5599-9eae-86f82aec85f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094796} {:answer/id #uuid "f914470b-dc52-52fd-977b-65814c410cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 3 + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094797} {:answer/id #uuid "3208ddc6-452f-5f4f-bfef-252a124463b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094798} {:answer/id #uuid "45323c64-e7df-59cc-84f6-49f89ffab9e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094799} {:answer/id #uuid "70fe78d5-79ed-559e-ab74-f865abba7a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln 3} + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094800}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6bb3288b-51b9-54b1-8b95-4333cd4a102b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094795}] :question/id #uuid "55e0676e-8226-56ea-844c-41bb8f4c2189" :question/math-academy-id "q-17395" :question/problem "Given that $y = \\log_{3} x + 5\\ln x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x = 1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ae057d0-d78b-5718-aa6f-daab4feb4650" :question/math-academy-id "q-101723" :question/problem "Given that $y=4{e}^{x}-3{log}_{7}x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}7}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope  of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}7})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{3}{3\\operatorname{ln}7} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c8b4247-2f6e-5c89-84d3-05e82fd928d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c8b4247-2f6e-5c89-84d3-05e82fd928d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232814} :answer-field/id #uuid "b23a283b-6469-55b9-90b7-faa54b42b98a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "203042d7-3a90-5b98-a3a8-41d259d10f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-340014" :question/problem "Given the function $y=5{x}^{2}+6\\operatorname{ln}x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=3$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2}+6\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2x+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =10x+\\frac{6}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(10x+\\frac{6}{x})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 3+\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =32\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe3da45a-b176-52b2-a1fc-b27d861de6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}-18\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe3da45a-b176-52b2-a1fc-b27d861de6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}-18\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232816} :answer-field/id #uuid "263e1f60-7948-5f00-a01d-0963d8a18442" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7cc61275-8b03-5f03-bb68-53ecece9ebf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-340022" :question/problem "Given the function $y=5\\operatorname{ln}x-2\\cdot {3}^{x},$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{ln}x-2\\cdot {3}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}-2\\cdot {3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}3 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{5}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{x})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-18\\operatorname{ln}3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a68429f7-6205-5d83-9b54-817cfb429a93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232820} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1498cc-e778-47a5-bb1a-c239ac9e2a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3e^2+\\frac{1}{\\ln4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a68429f7-6205-5d83-9b54-817cfb429a93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232820} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb82ad2c-5850-514d-a61d-c6dc21f1e26a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25397da2-818c-507a-82b9-e23dda017608" :question/math-academy-id "q-340109" :question/problem "Given the function $y=-3{e}^{x}+2{log}_{4}x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{e}^{x}+2{log}_{4}x) \\\\  & =-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}x) \\\\  & =-3{e}^{x}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}4} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}4})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{2}{2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}4} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e390b863-0cc7-5db5-bfcb-f1828e76e02e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70897" :question/problem "Given that $y=2{log}_{2}x+{2}^{x}$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}2\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}2)|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}2}+4\\operatorname{ln}2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "472e11dd-8537-5b30-ad11-59c4c14c5212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236273} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4f0ac8-1dab-5270-b011-493f700ff938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+8ln⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236509} {:answer/id #uuid "78e82567-e2b5-51dd-885b-f1af7319339c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236577} {:answer/id #uuid "90cac687-dd21-570e-a62a-f9e1d628421a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8ln⁡2-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236739} {:answer/id #uuid "97421f7d-e972-5d83-b422-5d436b8e6feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78e82567-e2b5-51dd-885b-f1af7319339c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236577} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e2000d3-5ddf-572d-be68-d0feed75463e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09ca9b0e-b19f-5aca-b14f-466e3c4366f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-101726" :question/problem "Given that $y=3x-5+8{log}_{2}⁡x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-5+8{log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-5)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5)+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =3-0+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{8}{xln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1/ln⁡2} & ={(3+\\frac{8}{xln⁡2})|}_{x=1/ln⁡2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{8}{(\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}\\cdot ln⁡2)} \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ea60620-2ab9-5040-8270-703c9a1d6b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281818} {:answer/id #uuid "7936ae4e-f008-5af5-820c-1674250b0ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282726} {:answer/id #uuid "7c387048-20f2-5147-a642-ff8e502ef022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282760} {:answer/id #uuid "90f5b318-f4a9-5268-90ba-ba237d66d663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282944} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3d6901-3436-54f0-a0b1-ce4e806a253f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ea60620-2ab9-5040-8270-703c9a1d6b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281818} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec15cdba-b1f7-5ecd-9880-c9e9cda591f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9bd05e5a-ceb5-5b6d-a1ee-24c21df80b24" :question/math-academy-id "q-17371" :question/problem "Given that $y=3ln⁡x+2{x}^{2}-5x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3ln⁡x+2{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3ln⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+4x-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{x}+4x-5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{3}{x}+4x-5)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}+4\\cdot 1-5 \\\\  & =3+4-5 \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42c897e4-b652-55dd-8d72-bc5035453929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-\\frac{5}{2\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42c897e4-b652-55dd-8d72-bc5035453929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-\\frac{5}{2\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312506} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f3d565-6897-5bcf-9632-a037dba3624d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1eb887e7-89db-539c-9d35-d652e9bb15c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-340024" :question/problem "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}-5{log}_{3}⁡x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-5{log}_{3}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{3}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{xln⁡3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(6{x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{xln⁡3})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =6(2)^{2}-\\frac{5}{2ln⁡3} \\\\  & =24-\\frac{5}{2ln⁡3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101f0087-1aec-50e5-a9b7-d806a0ea860a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "101f0087-1aec-50e5-a9b7-d806a0ea860a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312090} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a7fc2dd-1d62-5a23-a97f-19baf25d47a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b69d4c2-7ebc-59ed-aa14-566d23bb3592" :question/math-academy-id "q-340026" :question/problem "Given the function $y=6{log}_{2}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-3x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=1$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{log}_{2}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-3x) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x)+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2}+4\\cdot 2x-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{xln⁡2}+8x-3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{6}{xln⁡2}+8x-3)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1\\cdot ln⁡2}+8(1)-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{ln⁡2}+5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60475637-df2c-5099-a5a7-9cd23687c0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60475637-df2c-5099-a5a7-9cd23687c0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312747} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bd5a890-600f-5ed0-9892-4e5fc04515a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c352abb-1992-52cb-94e7-b48e48f5bbc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-340110" :question/problem "Given the function $y=4{e}^{x}-3{log}_{2}⁡x+7,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=3$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}-3{log}_{2}⁡x+7) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7) \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2}+0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{xln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{xln⁡2})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot ln⁡2} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c631962-dd2a-53db-b827-84d94e8f7e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403414} {:answer/id #uuid "8f33e14e-f91d-5c5f-9b34-7c61ede2d34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403415} {:answer/id #uuid "33140677-5da7-59ef-8215-135fba67dffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403416} {:answer/id #uuid "7fefc24f-ce9e-58b5-aba2-9f2cb372222e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403417} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3a5a72-8cb5-5f5c-812b-2114a27a36be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f33e14e-f91d-5c5f-9b34-7c61ede2d34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403415} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fcab4c2-5aab-5cee-8699-609d2431de61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ddfac57c-89c4-597b-b080-b0ac4a48d4c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-70903" :question/problem "Given that $y=3\\operatorname{log}⁡x+{x}^{3}-4$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+3{x}^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+3{x}^{2})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+3\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+27\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}]}
